WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.010
1,200 years since Emperor Kammu settled 
on a location for the palace...

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:11.020
These days 1.5 million humans 
live in the city of Kyoto.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.320
But wait, one moment.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.030
"Humans, they're naught but an 
accompaniment to our history.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.200
We were the ones who built 
history, and this city,"

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.350
say some big-talking tanuki.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.420
But wait, one moment.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.420
"The skies above the palace have been 
our territory since ancient times.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.690
Fear and respect us who 
dwell in the heavens,"

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.980
someone arrogantly opined.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.930
A tengu.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.650
Humans live in the city, 
tanuki crawl the earth,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.860
tengu fly through the air.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.890
Since the Heian era relocation, humans, tanuki, 
and tengu have maintained a delicate balance.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.160
That's what keeps the great wheel of 
this city turning round and round.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:10.620
More fun than anything is 
watching that wheel spin.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:19.350
I'm what you'd call a tanuki, 
but too proud to be a <i>mere</i> tanuki,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.120
I admire tengu from afar 
and love imitating humans.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.410
For that reason, my daily 
life is so dizzyingly busy

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.410
there's no time to be bored.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.950
<b>Episode One: 
Goddess of the Noryoyuka</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.260
<b>25th Shimogamo Summer Used Book Fair, 
August 11th (Sun.) - 16 (Fri.)</b>

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:23.580
Big brother!

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.460
Going around looking like that again!

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:32.890
If you keep changing forms all the 
time, Yaichiro'll scold you again.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.710
Tanuki societal norms can 
eat dirt for all I care.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.620
But hey, did you need something?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.160
You're going to Prof. Akadama's place, right?

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.310
Mom said to use this.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.030
<b>Demachi shopping arcade Masugata</b>

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.250
She said she found it on the ground 
in the ticket office at the station.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.260
Don't tell me this is actually a leaf...

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:07.460
See you later.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.140
<b>Demachi shopping arcade Masugata</b>

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.930
What's <i>with</i> you?! I'll scream!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.710
Pervert!

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.260
Quit messing around!

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:59.610
What are you suppose to be? Even 
just looking at you is embarrassing.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.500
So don't look then.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.180
Don't quibble!

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.930
If you think of it as a favor 
to our master, Prof. Akadama--

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.410
Shut up!

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.260
We're already branded as it is,

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:16.960
as the regrettable children who failed to 
inherit the blood of Shimogamo Soichiro.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:24.790
Just be good until after the 
Nise-emon election, got it?

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:39.890
Your daughter?

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.540
My younger brother.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.440
You airhead!

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.930
You really think such a cheap 
trick would make me happy?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:00.680
Professor, it's precisely for your sake that, 
as you rot away here day after day,

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.630
as a breath of fresh air for your stale life--

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.490
I have no interest in seeing 
your alluring figure!

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.550
Are you unable to comprehend the degree of 
artistry achieved in this transformation?

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:14.690
Behold! The swell of this perfect chest,

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:18.100
the slenderness of these hips, 
all the rest of this pert--

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.400
Cut it out, don't be weird.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.820
You mean you can't forgive 
yourself for getting turned on?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.190
In that case you're barking up the 
wrong tree getting mad at me.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.490
I won't be made a fool by the likes of you.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:33.990
Of all the impuden--

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.270
I bought you a bento.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.210
Please eat it.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.620
Have you seen Benten lately?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.980
No, haven't seen her in a while.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.090
She hasn't come around here in a long time.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.850
I wonder how she's doing, wherever she is.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:09.410
There's no way she'd want to 
come back to a place like this.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:10.560
Is that so?

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.670
For me, it's still impossible.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.460
What's all this then?

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.810
Here before you is one

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.330
Yasaburo, third son of Shimogawa Soichiro.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.430
I come bearing a gift for 
Nyoigatake Yakushibo.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.160
My thanks.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.110
You shouldn't have gone to such trouble.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.790
What are you wearing?

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.550
Is it weird?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.310
So you're not human either, huh.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.860
Hm, we'll have to see about that. And you?

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.300
I'm just a Suzuki Satomi.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.530
Leave him be, don't tease.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.140
He's sly, that one - a nasty fellow.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.910
He seems interesting!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.540
Him, interesting?

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:20.030
He's a clever one - capable, but 
knows nothing of self improvement.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.640
He'll never amount to anything.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.910
He seems to be quite fond of you.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.500
Don't be absurd.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.700
Would you like to see the flowers?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.250
I've never seen such a splendid cherry tree.

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:44.610
Hey,

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.090
why don't you try doing what I taught you.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.840
But I can't yet.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.870
Give it a try.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.340
I did it!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.160
To be a tengu is

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.960
to fly through the sky at will.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:38.330
Awful, awful! I can't 
believe I just ate that.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.110
Let's get this place's bento again next time.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.170
You ate half of it so it must 
not have been that bad.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:50.300
Is that any way to treat your master?

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.500
"I'll just get this over with cheaply," psh.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.810
Today is Friday.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:03.080
I dare say Benten is out 
with The Friday Fellows.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.330
She must be having a good time.

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:10.080
What's so fun about hanging 
around those humans?

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:14.500
Benten's human, too. Had you forgotten?

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.600
She's always out partying at night...

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.330
If I don't keep an eye on her she 
immediately strays down the path of evil.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.110
Oh well.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:27.080
Don't you think "strays down the path 
of evil" is a strange way to put...

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.250
Shush!

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.190
This place airs out better than you'd think.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.980
Pretty much the only ones who come 
around here are you and the bugs.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.540
How dreary.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.070
I'd like to be given a bit of thanks.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.850
Who asked you to come?

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.580
You were such a troublesome student.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.390
I was finally rid of the chore 
of seeing that mug of yours

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.500
and now I'm supposed to be happy 
when you nonchalantly drop by?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.180
I'm fresh out of lectures!

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:14.060
Wouldn't you say that the worse the 
student, the more you love them, Prof?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:17.900
Who said that?! Idiot...

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.700
Since you've got nothing better to do,

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.120
go find Benten and bring her here.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:33.060
No way. Even if I try to 
persuade her she won't come.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.840
Besides, I loath both Benten 
and The Friday Fellows.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.820
Also, while you're out 
please pick up some Q-tips.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.270
When my ears are itchy I'm 
liable to unleash a whirlwind.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.770
There is a new package of 
Q-tips on the washstand.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:49.340
Haven't I been saying I'm not going to go?

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:52.830
Wait one moment, I think I'll write a letter.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.790
Hmm, Ben, ben, ten, ten...

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.370
You stubborn old tengu!

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:58.840
Quietly clean out your ears and get to bed!

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.240
Err, it'd be better to use her real name here...

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.680
What was it again?

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.070
<b>To Suzuki Satomi</b>

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.460
Make sure that you deliver 
this to Benten tonight.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.680
Consider this your honorable duty.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:17.210
I, Shimogamo Yasaburo, accept this mission.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.560
Right!

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.760
This is just the prop for Cupid.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.030
<b>Demachi 
shopping arcade {smp: I adjusted the placement and style of these so they are actually aligned with the labels. luckily i had a friend nearby who can read a little japanese and we figured it out. But for the next time, you can just drag stuff to change their placement by selecting that blue four-way directional arrow on the lefthand column of icons next to the video, and then dragging the little squares above each line.}</b>

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.030
<b>Chikurintei</b>

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.030
<b>Masugata Co-op</b>

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.750
Seven Lucky Gods, Seven Lucky Gods...

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.880
That... must be them?

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.320
But I don't see the essential...

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:07.850
There she is!

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:19.340
Of all people, Nyoigatake Yakushibo...

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:23.470
it's exactly as if he's a 
day-dreaming high school idiot.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.800
One shot like a modern-day Nasu no Yoichi!

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.050
Who's there?

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.610
Are you okay?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:54.640
Yikes!

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.140
How awful!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:07.240
<b>Akegarasu</b>

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.590
This is no place for a young la--

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:12.830
It's me, it's me.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.820
Oh <i>you</i>, sheesh.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.910
Going around looking like that again!

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.280
These powers were bestowed 
exclusively upon us,

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.250
so what's wrong with me 
using them however I like?

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:24.600
If you're so good at shape-shifting,

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:28.100
you could at least take on an 
appropriate form when you come here.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.540
An Electric Brandy.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.150
I'll have an Aka 'n Shochu.

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:39.870
What was all that about 
earlier? You startled me.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.730
The professor told me to deliver 
the love letter, so I did.

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:49.560
You were all the way across the river, so 
I took the liberty of sending it by arrow.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.640
Are you looking for a fight?

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.920
I guess you could call it 
a token of my love-hate.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.410
I enjoy making sure people 
looking for fights find them.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.380
I'm okay, thanks.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:09.820
You ruined my precious fan and The 
Friday Fellows are in an uproar.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:13.440
I said I wasn't feeling well and left.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:17.130
If I had really wanted 
to hit you, I would have.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.070
I bet!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.750
Thwack, right through my eyeball.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:27.670
My apologies about the 
fan. If you like, I can--

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.670
No thanks, I'll be holding on to this.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.290
That love letter... did you read it?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.450
Yeah, the professor is 
getting all worked up again?

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.560
Fretting and fretting - he's 
becoming impossible to deal with.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:49.710
Right? Well I haven't been back in so long.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.930
Couldn't you try to go at least once a week?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.850
I don't want you to meddle in this.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:00.140
I don't have any intention of 
poking my nose into it, either.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.670
Not even a dog would sniff that.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.320
He says, even though he's a "raccoon dog."

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.770
I don't suppose you go for tanuki...

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.670
I'm a human, what can you expect?

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:20.960
But if you're looking for a 
fight, I'll find one for you.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:22.460
Terrific.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.130
Then I'll catch you and make you 
into a stew for our year-end bash.

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:28.200
Always so unreasonable.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:30.820
It's a Friday Fellows custom.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:35.040
At the end of every year we 
stew a tanuki and eat it.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.740
Bartender, another round.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.710
By the way,

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.510
why are you looking so cute today?

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:50.040
I thought I would add some flavor 
to the professor's daily life.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.140
I got her to look pretty cute, right?

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.870
A beautiful display of master-disciple love.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.900
You'd think, but I got a good scolding.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:02.720
That selfish old tengu. 
You can just leave him be.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.160
No, I can't do that.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.190
The Demon King Cedar 
incident is getting to you?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.150
It doesn't bother you, I take it.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.330
What should bother me?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.040
It's our fault the professor 
can't fly anymore.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.690
You were the one who 
transformed into the cedar.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:26.730
And then the professor 
fell and hurt his back.

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.370
But you were the one who 
came up with the plan!

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.110
Yeah, and?

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:38.180
This is what makes you a human, I guess. 
You guys are way worse than tengu.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.500
I'm sorry to say,

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:45.350
but you don't understand the 
professor's feelings one bit.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.660
Minamiza. That's where the professor is.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:58.240
You don't know whether I'm 
going to meet him or not.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:01.130
I'm sorry to have presum--

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.440
How you even managed to stay 
alive this long is beyond me.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.470
This is what I live for.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.330
<b>Shijo Ohashi</b>

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.830
Professor...

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.550
you got a lot of nerve.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.850
Wait a second.

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:58.300
I'm about to stand up, and if you don't 
mind, I'll wrap my arms around you.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:04.000
And then if you don't mind, well I think the 
two of us might take a leisurely mid-air stroll.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.540
You shouldn't offer to do things 
you clearly can't, Master.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:12.620
Ah.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.510
Oh, Professor.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.690
What are you doing here?

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:38.910
Oh, it's you.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:41.160
Drunk, huh.

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.120
I did have a bit to drink.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:46.540
Always screwing around, you are.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.880
Well, I'm going to call it a night.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:52.960
W-Wait, I'm going home, 
too, so hail us a taxi.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:57.780
Professor, I think a quick flight 
would be faster than a taxi, but?

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:04.370
Please don't be spiteful.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:09.080
How pathetic, my back hurts 
so much I can't even move.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:21.310
You idiot, haven't I told you 
to cut out the maiden look?

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:24.590
It looks like a granddaughter has 
come to pick up her grandfather.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.740
You still haven't told me what 
you were doing over there...?

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:40.340
Yes, well, sometimes I like 
to have a drink in Gion.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:41.860
Is that so?

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:53.540
To be a tengu is to fly 
through the sky at will...

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:55.830
wouldn't you say?

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.280
But there's nothing wrong with 
taking a taxi now and then.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.780
Yes, nothing wrong.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.830
Even I get sick of transforming sometimes.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:15.050
Are you lumping me together 
with you hairballs?

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:17.880
Once,

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.210
I wrestled with the difficult question 
of how one should live as a tanuki.

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:26.630
I felt I understood how to 
live an interesting life, but

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:31.150
it was unclear what else I should do.

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:35.370
And then, somewhere along the line, 
idling away my time doing nothing,

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:40.760
I realized that there's 
nothing else I need to do

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:42.380
besides live an interesting life.

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:35.010
Big brother, oh no! The 
god of thunder is coming!

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.290
We have to hurry and let mom know!

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Mom and Raijin, God of Thunder</b>
